From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jert <joseph96tb@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:59:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx179, imx362: let the sensors idle after probe

Both drivers take a pm_runtime_get_noresume() at the end of probe and never
drop it, so the sensor is powered from probe to unbind. Measured on taimen:
that, venus and Easel together are 48.3 mA of a screen-off idle -- about
244 mW -- and the two sensors are the largest share of it, pinning
CAMSS_TOP and the CCI device with them.

The comment that justified the hold is stale. It dodges
clk_prepare_enable() on MCLK1 returning -EBUSY once CAMSS_TOP has
collapsed, and imx179_power_on() already solves that directly: it holds
the CCI device -- which owns CAMSS_TOP -- awake across the sensor's whole
power cycle, and imx362_power_on() does the same.

Dropping the hold also fixes a functional bug the imx179 s_stream comment
describes: with the part never powered down, nothing re-initialises it
between streams, so only the FIRST stream attempt after a boot works.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c | 18 +++++++++---------
 drivers/media/i2c/imx362.c |  4 ++--
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c
index 2ae417b15037..406faed16db8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c
@@ -1136,18 +1136,18 @@ static int imx179_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * Deliberately NO pm_runtime_idle() here yet: probe already powered the
-	 * sensor up, and letting it idle straight back down exposes a resume
-	 * path that currently fails -- clk_prepare_enable() on MCLK1 returns
-	 * -EBUSY once CAMSS_TOP has collapsed, which puts the device into
-	 * runtime-PM error state and makes every later get return -EBUSY
-	 * ("Resource busy" out of VIDIOC_STREAMON). Holding power from probe
-	 * keeps first light independent of that bug; it costs idle power and
-	 * must not survive past bring-up.
+	 * Let it idle straight back down. The resume path this used to dodge
+	 * -- clk_prepare_enable() on MCLK1 returning -EBUSY with CAMSS_TOP
+	 * collapsed -- is handled in imx179_power_on() now, which holds the CCI
+	 * device (the one that owns CAMSS_TOP) awake across the sensor's whole
+	 * power cycle. Holding the sensor runtime-active from probe instead
+	 * cost idle power for the life of the boot, and left the part powered
+	 * but never re-initialised, so only the FIRST stream after a boot
+	 * worked.
 	 */
 	pm_runtime_set_active(dev);
-	pm_runtime_get_noresume(dev);
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
+	pm_runtime_idle(dev);
 
 	return 0;
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx362.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx362.c
index 0e0779d49eec..7fad5ef406ed 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx362.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx362.c
@@ -1098,10 +1098,10 @@ static int imx362_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_media_cleanup;
 
-	/* Same runtime-PM hold as imx179 -- see the comment there. */
+	/* Idles straight back down -- see the comment in imx179_probe(). */
 	pm_runtime_set_active(dev);
-	pm_runtime_get_noresume(dev);
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
+	pm_runtime_idle(dev);
 
 	return 0;
 
